@startuml
title BCS compiler: an IOP becomes a hash-based SNARK
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  ParticipantBorderColor #7A5BB5
  LifeLineBorderColor #7A5BB5
  ArrowColor #7A5BB5
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
}

participant "Prover P(x, w)" as P
participant "Verifier V(x)" as V

P -> V : Merkle root of string pi_0
V -> P : challenge alpha_1
P -> V : Merkle root of string pi_1
V -> P : challenge alpha_2
P -> V : ... Merkle root of string pi_k
note over P, V #F3EEFB
  Fiat-Shamir: each alpha_i is replaced by a hash
  of the Merkle roots sent so far, so P runs the
  whole exchange alone and the proof becomes
  non-interactive.
end note
V -> P : query cell j of pi_i
P -> V : value pi_i[j] + Merkle authentication path
V -> V : run the IOP decision algorithm\non the opened cells; accept or reject
note over V
  Proof size = k + 1 Merkle roots
  + one Merkle path per query.
  Fewer queries means a shorter proof.
end note
@enduml
